  "html": "<p class=\"\">For presentations and livestreaming: show every key you press as large ASCII art on screen, so an audience can follow along.</p>\n<p class=\"\">This was a fun \"can robots make TUIs?\" experiment. Answer: they can, and it's fun. The idea was to have it open in a tmux pane while I work — especially vim stuff, where people wanna know your shortcuts — but I clearly don't use it; I have like 250 GitHub repos now. The question got answered, and that was the point.</p>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"showtouch displaying a keystroke as full-screen centered ASCII art\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/showtouch/demo.png\" alt=\"showtouch displaying a keystroke as full-screen centered ASCII art\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/projects/showtouch/demo.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/projects/showtouch/demo.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/showtouch/demo.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/projects/showtouch/demo.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"showtouch displaying a keystroke as full-screen centered ASCII art\" width=\"1750\" height=\"1880\" style=\"--splay-rot:-1.16deg;\" data-dimensions=\"1750×1880\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm img-splay aspect-square w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">showtouch displaying a keystroke as full-screen centered ASCII art</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"How it works — pynput captures keys, pyfiglet renders them as centered ASCII art\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/showtouch/code.png\" alt=\"How it works — pynput captures keys, pyfiglet renders them as centered ASCII art\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/projects/showtouch/code.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/projects/showtouch/code.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/showtouch/code.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/projects/showtouch/code.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"How it works — pynput captures keys, pyfiglet renders them as centered ASCII art\" width=\"1400\" height=\"900\" style=\"--splay-rot:-2.45deg;\" data-dimensions=\"1400×900\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm img-splay w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">How it works — pynput captures keys, pyfiglet renders them as centered ASCII art</figcaption>\n</figure>",
